course: dictionary
lesson: 2875
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Donor is one of them: it can mean a person who gives money or help, a person who gives blood or an organ, or something in science. The words around it tell you which meaning is being used.
explain: «There are never enough donors: people needing a new kidney often wait for years.» The clues are kidney, organ and sick. So here a donor is someone who gives an organ to help a sick person.
explain: «A generous donor» gives money or help to a cause, such as a school fundraiser. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word, and check it still makes sense.
fact: Donor is a noun, and donors is the plural.
fact: A donor is someone who gives something to help others, such as money, goods, help, blood or an organ.
fact: «A blood donor» gives blood, and «an organ donor» gives a healthy organ, such as the heart, kidneys, liver, lungs or corneas.
fact: One donor can save or improve the lives of several people; the NHS says up to nine.
fact: In science, a donor is something that gives up a part, such as an atom giving an electron.
exercise: «There are never enough donors: people needing a new kidney often wait for years.» What does donor mean here? | A person who sells cars | A person who sings in a choir | A person who reads the news | *A person who gives an organ to help someone who is sick
exercise: «A generous donor» gives money or help to a cause. What does donor mean in this phrase? | A person who takes things away from charities | *A person who gives money or help to a cause | A person who gives out prizes at school | A person who is always late
exercise: «Families of donors and people who received organs can write thank-you letters to each other.» Find and copy one word that means got or was given. | families | *received | letters | donors
test: In science, what is a donor? | A sort of cell found only in plants | A kind of medicine that cures colds | *Something that gives up a part, such as an atom giving an electron | Something that takes in light and glows
test: «In England, adults are counted as willing donors unless they have said no.» What does this mean? | Only children can be donors | Nobody is ever asked about organ donation | *Most adults are willing to give organs unless they have said no | Adults must pay money to become donors
exam: Which phrase means a person who gives money to a charity? | a blood donor | *a generous donor | a science donor | an organ donor
